# 17. Glossary of Key Terms

## Purpose

This glossary defines key terms used throughout the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) Project Charter. These definitions establish a common engineering vocabulary and promote consistency across all engineering documentation.

---

### Adaptive

The capability of a system to modify or coordinate its behavior in response to changing operating conditions while remaining aligned with defined objectives and constraints.

---

### Architecture

The fundamental organization of a system, including its elements, relationships, interactions, and governing principles.

---

### Constraint

A condition, limitation, or boundary within which engineering decisions and system development must occur.

---

### Engineering Knowledge

The documented collection of engineering principles, analyses, decisions, models, architectures, requirements, and validation evidence produced throughout the project.

---

### Governance

The framework of principles, policies, roles, and processes used to guide and control the development and evolution of the project.

---

### Objective

A defined engineering outcome that the project or system is intended to achieve.

---

### Requirement

A verifiable statement describing a capability, condition, or performance that the engineered system must satisfy.

---

### Stakeholder

An individual, group, or organization that influences, contributes to, benefits from, or is affected by the project.

---

### Traceability

The ability to establish and maintain documented relationships between objectives, requirements, architectures, engineering decisions, analyses, and validation activities.

---

### Validation

The process of demonstrating, through objective evidence, that the engineered system satisfies its intended objectives and stakeholder needs.

---

### Verification

The process of confirming, through objective evidence, that engineering outputs satisfy their specified requirements.

---

### Baseline

A formally approved version of a document or engineering artifact that serves as the reference point for future development and controlled change.
